Q: Calculating ComboBox DropDownWidth in C# A: <pre><code>private void AdjustWidthComboBox_DropDown(object sender, System.EventArgs e)
{
    ComboBox senderComboBox = (ComboBox)sender;
    int width = senderComboBox.DropDownWidth;
    Graphics g = senderComboBox.CreateGraphics();
    Font font = senderComboBox.Font;
    int vertScrollBarWidth = 
        (senderComboBox.Items.Count&gt;senderComboBox.MaxDropDownItems)
        ?SystemInformation.VerticalScrollBarWidth:0;

    int newWidth;
    foreach (string s in ((ComboBox)sender).Items)
    {
        newWidth = (int) g.MeasureString(s, font).Width + vertScrollBarWidth;
        if (width &lt; newWidth )
        {
            width = newWidth;
        }
    }
    senderComboBox.DropDownWidth = width;
}
</code></pre>

Q: Auto-generated GRPC classes aren&#39;t accessible as source folders in EclipseIDE, but exist A: <p>The fix is to declare the classpath as source-folder before the buildship plugin can overwrite the changes by using <code>file.beforeMerged {}</code> instead of <code>file.whenMerged {}</code>. The following change resolved the issue:</p>
<pre><code>eclipse {
    classpath {
        file.beforeMerged { cp -&gt;
            cp.entries.add(
                new org.gradle.plugins.ide.eclipse.model.SourceFolder(
                    'build/generated/source/proto/main/grpc', null))
            cp.entries.add(
                new org.gradle.plugins.ide.eclipse.model.SourceFolder(
                    'build/generated/source/proto/main/java', null))
        }
    }
}
</code></pre>

Q: passport&#39;s req.isAuthenticated always returning false, even when I hardcode done(null, true) A: <p>So, if you tried all of the above, and it still doesn't doesn't fix this, as it was for me, try tweaking your session settings, and checking if the cookie isn't getting deleted when the user gets redirected by chance.</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>app.use( 
  session({
    secret: &quot;my_secret&quot;,
    resave: false,
    saveUninitialized: true,
    cookie: { secure: true },
   // ^
   // | this is what was breaking it for me 
}));
</code></pre>
<p>i don't really know why this was causing it, but i realized that the cookie was being deleted whenever i got redirected to the page, hence isAuthenticated always returned false. After deleting this line everything started working as intended. I think i should add that i am very new to express and javascript in general and i am not entirely sure what this line even does, i just saw it somewhere on the internet as an example and i just added it without thinking about it too much. So i guess my advice would be to never add random things you don't understand to your code without checking what they do and if you even need them at all...</p>
